        "name": "USN-5179-2",
        "description": "USN-5179-1 fixed vulnerabilities in BusyBox. This update provides the corresponding updates for Ubuntu 16.04 ESM.  Original advisory details:   It was discovered that BusyBox incorrectly handled certain malformed gzip  archives. If a user or automated system were tricked into processing a  specially crafted gzip archive, a remote attacker could use this issue to  cause BusyBox to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly  execute arbitrary code. (CVE-2021-28831)",
        "aliases": [
          "CVE-2021-28831"
        ]
      },
